ReadBoot Branding Standards
1. Visual direction
Aesthetic: High-contrast, editorial, **magazine-leaning** layout—**full-bleed and seamless** flow by default. **Do not** treat heavy **ruled boxes** or thick outer frames on every block as the default; use lighter separation (space, type, image) unless a design explicitly calls for a frame.

Linework: **Color tokens are unchanged** (charcoal, crimson, etc.). **Do not** default to thick border treatment on all primary containers and buttons—borders are intentional accents, not universal chrome.

Corner Radius: Prefer **12px** rounded corners when rounding is used (`$ref-border-radius`-aligned tokens when defined).

2. Design Tokens (Source of Truth)
**New work:** use tokens from `packages/ui/src/Tokens/**` (`@use "Tokens/…"` from Framework or component `.module.scss`). **Legacy** until migrated: `packages/ui/src/patterns/Atoms/**`. Do not hardcode brand colors.

Colors (unchanged):

Paper Background: $sys-color-paper-bg (#FAF9F6)

Ink/Text: $sys-color-ink-text (#36454F)

Action Primary: $sys-color-action-primary (#DC143C)

Typography:

Headlines: Baloo 2 (Weight: 700).

Body: Inter (Academic/Clean).

3. Interactive Effects
Hover States: Interactive elements may use subtle motion (e.g. modest scale + easing)—avoid mandatory “bouncy” scale on every control unless specified.

Long-form body copy: **column-count** is optional; prefer layout-driven columns where the design calls for it (no blanket mandate).

Note: "The Glitch" effect is officially deprecated and has been removed from the system. Do NOT apply .fx--glitch.

4. Technical Requirements
Format: Use SCSS Modules (.module.scss) exclusively for component styling in `@repo/ui`. No CSS-in-JS or Styled-Components.

SCSS Modules: `@use` token modules from `packages/ui/src/Tokens/**` in component `.module.scss` files (legacy paths under `patterns/Atoms/**` until removed). See **`readboot-scss-architecture.mdc`**.

5. Editorial vocabulary (still SSOT for words)
Use **`readboot-newspaper-terminology.mdc`** for **language** in Storybook `parameters.docs`, UI comments, and marketing copy (kicker, deck, lead, full-bleed, etc.)—it applies to **magazine-style** and legacy UIs. **Glossary terms are not a mandate** to add boxed chrome; they name patterns for humans.

Legacy hero components (`BoxedFeatureHero`, `FullBleedHero`, `ReadBootBand`) remain valid **code names** where those files exist; **greenfield** work favors **full-bleed / minimal outer rules** per §1.
